  "body": "Fixes #876\n\n## Summary\n\n* **What is the goal of this PR?** Replace the current synthetic `Tab Row N, Cell N:` paragraphs with a lightweight column layout for the simple tables commonly found in EPUBs.\n* **What changes are included?**\n  - Renders rows with 2-4 simple cells as equal-width positioned columns using the existing `PageLine` and `PageHorizontalRule` primitives.\n  - Keeps `<th>` text bold, respects cell text alignment/direction, mirrors column order for RTL rows, preserves image alt text, and accounts for native ruby height when advancing table rows.\n  - Falls back to ordinary full-width flow when a row is too narrow or complex: more than four cells, more than 32 words or 512 text bytes in a cell, an internal link, or other unsupported structure. Content is preserved rather than truncated.\n  - Flattens nested-table text into the enclosing cell without creating recursive table state.\n  - Bumps `section.bin` to version 38 so existing cached word positions are rebuilt once; version 37 is used by current `develop`.\n\n\n\n## Additional Context\n\n### Intentionally limited scope\n\nThis is a deliberately smaller alternative to #2533 and follows the maintainer direction in #2278 to start with simple table cases without border/CSS machinery. Those are also the limited cases CrossInk supports, as noted in [the same discussion](https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader/pull/2278#issuecomment-4640473055), and match the [maintainer request](https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader/pull/2278#issuecomment-4640297495) for a reviewable core implementation.\n\nThe implementation does **not** add a table block type, new page serialization tags, CSS border parsing, intrinsic column sizing, `colspan`, or `rowspan`. Unsupported rows keep the existing readable stacked behavior, so those can be added incrementally if there is demand.\n\nGrid borders are intentionally kept in the separate follow-up #2954.\n\n### Memory and firmware impact\n\nThe parser buffers only the active row. The row vector is pre-reserved for four cells; each grid cell is bounded to 32 words and 512 text bytes before the row switches to streaming full-width flow. `ParsedText` cells are allocated with `makeUniqueNoThrow` because they must survive across Expat callbacks; stack lifetime is insufficient and static storage would make parser instances share mutable state.\n\nCompared with `origin/develop` at `d0359edf` using clean `default` builds and the same submodule revisions:\n\n| Metric | `develop` | This PR | Delta |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Static DRAM | 119,021 B | 119,021 B | 0 B |\n| PlatformIO RAM | 52,036 B | 52,036 B | 0 B |\n| Firmware image | 5,503,841 B | 5,507,667 B | +3,826 B |\n\n### Validation\n\n- Current GitHub CI: firmware build, unit tests, cppcheck, clang-format, title check, and CodeRabbit all pass\n- `pio run -e default`: passed\n- `pio check -e default`: passed, no defects\n- Fresh host CMake/CTest build: 129/129 tests passed\n- `clang-format` and `git diff --check`: passed\n- Flashed to an Xteink X4 and tested with real three-column tables in *Momo* after a fresh section-cache rebuild:\n  - portrait and landscape\n  - Small and default Medium reader fonts\n  - default Medium portrait keeps the three cells on the same row\n  - no reset, OOM, or parser error observed while navigating the table pages\n\n### Known limitations\n\n- Equal-width columns only; no content-proportional sizing.\n- Grid mode supports at most four cells per row.\n- Narrow or complex rows intentionally render stacked.\n- No borders, `colspan`, `rowspan`, or table-specific CSS sizing.\n\n### Screenshots\n\nBefore/after screenshots from the Xteink X4, including portrait and landscape results, are in [this PR comment](https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader/pull/2654#issuecomment-5021045573).\n\n---\n\n### AI Usage\n\nDid you use AI tools to help write this code? **YES**\n\nImplemented and reviewed collaboratively with OpenAI Codex; the contributor performed the manual device and orientation/font validation.",
